# Custom Redaction Rules Schema

## Inline Rules (`.entire/settings.json`)

```json
{
  "redaction": {
    "custom_redactions": {
      "acme_token": "ACME_TOKEN_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}",
      "internal_id": "INTERNAL_[a-z]{6}_[0-9]{4}"
    }
  }
}
```

**Pattern syntax:** Uses Go RE2 regex; lookarounds and backreferences unavailable. Each entry produces a bare `REDACTED` token.

## Rule Packs (`.entire/redactors/` or `.entire/redactors/local/`)

```yaml
name: acme-internal
version: 1.0.0
description: Internal ACME service tokens
rules:
  - id: acme-token
    description: Long-lived ACME service tokens
    regex: 'ACME_TOKEN_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}'
    samples:
      - { input: "REDACTED", redacted: true }
      - { input: "ACME_TOKEN_short", redacted: false }
  - id: acme-session
    regex: 'asess_[a-f0-9]{32}'
```

**Required fields:** `name` (must match filename), `version`, and rules with `id` and `regex`. Supports `.yaml`, `.yml`, and `.json` formats. Labels become uppercased replacement tokens: `[REDACTED_<LABEL>]`.

## PII Configuration

```json
{
  "redaction": {
    "pii": {
      "enabled": true,
      "email": true,
      "phone": true,
      "address": false,
      "custom_patterns": {
        "employee_id": "EMP-\\d{6}"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Custom patterns:** Produce `[REDACTED_<LABEL>]` tokens using uppercased label names.

## Secret Scanner Engines

```json
{
  "redaction": {
    "betterleaks": {
      "enabled": true
    },
    "goredact": {
      "enabled": false
    }
  }
}
```

**Rules:** At least one scanner must remain enabled. Settings read only from `.entire/settings.json`, not local variants.

## OpenAI Privacy Filter (OPF)

```json
{
  "redaction": {
    "openai_privacy_filter": {
      "enabled": true,
      "categories": {
        "private_person": true,
        "private_email": true,
        "private_phone": true,
        "private_address": true,
        "private_url": true,
        "private_date": true,
        "account_number": true,
        "secret": true
      },
      "timeout_seconds": 30,
      "prompt_default": "ask",
      "command": "/opt/homebrew/bin/opf"
    }
  }
}
```

**Key notes:** At least one category required when enabled. `command` reads only from untracked `.entire/settings.local.json`. `prompt_default` accepts `"ask"`, `"always"`, or `"never"`.

